#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:5
#: e3b199ba023a4b4285548ebfef32b50c
msgid "PosHold Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:7
#: f412f5cc12f243b5b17a71399ba62708
msgid "The PosHold flight mode is similar to :ref:`Loiter <loiter-mode>` in that when the transmitter sticks are centered the vehicle maintains a constant location, heading, and altitude.  The major difference is that the pilot's roll and pitch inputs directly control the vehicle's lean angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:11
#: 94c7007489f942b1b602d309e432c5a7
msgid "In general :ref:`Loiter <loiter-mode>` is recommended over PosHold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:14
#: b0f00b1e4d864fc0b551d890edaca9be
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:16
#: bdf3e0f6396147d4acb501c233daf930
msgid "When switched on, PosHold mode will automatically attempts to maintain the current location, heading and altitude. Good GPS position, :ref:`low magnetic interference on the compass <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs_compass_interference>`\\ and :ref:`low vibrations <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs_vibrations>` are all important in achieving good loiter performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:26
#: 62d726bc580b46e9974787a8b11233c1
msgid "Controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:28
#: 6395398c1a4f44ad93d07bf9f225fd37
msgid "The pilot can control the copter's location horizontally and vertically with the control sticks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:31
#: 89e9fddff919464da29f38beb757ec20
msgid "Horizontal location can be adjusted with the Roll and Pitch control sticks with the default maximum lean angle being 45 degrees (angle can be adjusted with the :ref:`ATC_ANGLE_MAX<ATC_ANGLE_MAX>` parameter). When the pilot releases the sticks the copter will lean back to bring the vehicle to a stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:36
#: 0cf90b2a6b4542d19731c758c91bf931
msgid "Altitude can be controlled with the Throttle control stick just as in :ref:`AltHold mode <altholdmode_controls>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:38
#: 37bfe6d734464fbf9deed829971fed96
msgid "The heading can be set with the Yaw control stick"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:39
#: cb7535fc8ccd4e3ba13ce4885074e841
msgid "You may arm in PosHold mode but only once the GPS has 3D lock and the HDOP has dropped to 2.0 or lower."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:42
#: 9bc1efcde09f4abc917c9b193f8edd93
msgid "On a Pixhawk the LED will become green (:ref:`more details on LED patterns here <common-leds-pixhawk>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:44
#: dbe1b23c2a3140f8970bc897138ba381
msgid "The HDOP value can be made clearly visible through the mission planner's Quick screen by double clicking and then selecting \"gpshdop\" from the large grid of checkboxes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:51
#: 35c8a594eac7434f880b2c63bb41c28c
msgid "The maximum brake-angle can be set with the :ref:`PHLD_BRK_ANGLE<PHLD_BRK_ANGLE>` parameter (i.e. 30 = the vehicle will lean back up to 30degrees)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/poshold-mode.rst:53
#: c842a5747bcb4f55ae4dfdb65a088862
msgid "The speed the vehicle rotates back to the maximum angle can be set with the :ref:`PHLD_BRK_RATE<PHLD_BRK_RATE>` parameter (i.e. 8 = rotates back at 8 degrees per second))"
msgstr ""
